                        ],
                        "form": "die Offenbarungsreligionen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79997036-c00d-3b8b-9f9a-3186a44facaa",
                        "entry_id": "33002642-c251-3f79-ba75-ae0d016d7f0d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Religion, die sich in ihrem Selbstverständnis auf göttliche Offenbarungen beruft, auf diesen gründet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "84473802-a418-455c-a62e-41ab698e5692",
                                "sense_id": "79997036-c00d-3b8b-9f9a-3186a44facaa",
                                "text": "„Das Judentum ist eine Offenbarungsreligion; die Begegnung zwischen Gott und dem Volk auf dem Berg Sinai schuf ein gewisses Verständnis für das göttliche Tun, seine Gebote und seine Logik.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "33bd5325-6956-44f7-baf5-a38f69fe0821",
                        "source_entry_id": "33002642-c251-3f79-ba75-ae0d016d7f0d",
                        "source_sense_id": "79997036-c00d-3b8b-9f9a-3186a44facaa",
                        "source_sense_description": "Religion, die sich auf Offenbarungen beruft",
                        "target_lang_word": "revealed religion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "revealed religion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b08aa59d-2761-3041-89ef-bd78d3828d36",
                                        "entry_id": "b0022307-4ace-3d23-83a5-870b0e95eee5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The type of religion which relies on communication originating directly from a divine being (as reported by prophets, mystics, disciples, etc.) to establish what religious beliefs are authoritative and acceptable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "864f6419-e6ea-4f00-b25d-ac1a6806384a",
                                                "sense_id": "b08aa59d-2761-3041-89ef-bd78d3828d36",
                                                "text": "I am in no wise anxious to weaken the antithesis between natural and revealed religion. Science may help the former, but it has absolutely nothing to do with the latter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b5f65b6-9042-42f3-99ee-342e3402b3db",
                                                "sense_id": "b08aa59d-2761-3041-89ef-bd78d3828d36",
                                                "text": "I avowed outright my entire disbelief in the whole scheme of revealed religion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a00fd77d-27f2-415d-9387-b9670d509873",
                                                "sense_id": "b08aa59d-2761-3041-89ef-bd78d3828d36",
                                                "text": "The pope praised Cardinal Newman . . . for “his insights into the relationship between faith and reason, into the vital place of revealed religion in a civilized society.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8531fdf1-955e-363d-915f-b04423793ac1",
                                        "entry_id": "b0022307-4ace-3d23-83a5-870b0e95eee5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A particular system of religious beliefs based on such communication from a divine being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cba4f49-3479-4d15-a0af-0dfadb789d35",
                                                "sense_id": "8531fdf1-955e-363d-915f-b04423793ac1",
                                                "text": "Cicero . . . destroyed the whole revealed religion of the Greeks and Romans (for why should not theirs be a revealed religion as well as that of Christ?)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "653f9607-2f35-4ca0-8ef8-c75c634d99c5",
                                                "sense_id": "8531fdf1-955e-363d-915f-b04423793ac1",
                                                "text": "\"The more I study these objections, the less able I am to see how they come in conflict with belief in Christianity as a revealed religion.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9853250e-7816-4340-b7e2-516519c2fd51",
                                                "sense_id": "8531fdf1-955e-363d-915f-b04423793ac1",
                                                "text": "But very few of the world's real thinkers believe in revealed religions any more—they have come to see them simply as guesses of humanity at God's great sacred mystery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dce243c-90c4-46d2-9e6d-74761e026627",
                                                "sense_id": "8531fdf1-955e-363d-915f-b04423793ac1",
                                                "text": "[T]he fount of Islamic energy . . . : the desire to protect the purity of the Islamic faith and to vindicate its claim to be the final revealed religion on earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
